{"config":{"lang":["en"],"separator":"[\\s\\-]+","pipeline":["stopWordFilter"],"fields":{"title":{"boost":1000.0},"text":{"boost":1.0},"tags":{"boost":1000000.0}}},"docs":[{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-japanese/index.html","title":"Overview and preface","text":"Open TextbooksJapaneseA course in the Japanese languageWikibooks contributors <p>Open Textbooks</p> Japanese <p>A course in the Japanese language</p> <p>Wikibooks contributors</p> <p>Lessons in Japanese from the kana and first conversations to grammar, kanji and vocabulary.</p> Start reading <p>46 chapters</p>"},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-japanese/index.html#contents","title":"Contents","text":"<p>Chapters</p> <ul> <li>Chapter 1: Cover</li> </ul> <p>Introduction</p> <ul> <li>Chapter 2: About</li> <li>Chapter 3: Study methods</li> <li>Chapter 4: Contributor's Guide</li> <li>Chapter 5: Introduction</li> </ul> <p>Chapters</p> <ul> <li>Chapter 6: Practical Lessons</li> </ul> <p>Reading and writing</p> <ul> <li>Chapter 7: Japanese writing system</li> <li>Chapter 8: Kana</li> <li>Chapter 9: Kana chart</li> <li>Chapter 10: Kanji</li> <li>Chapter 11: Reader</li> <li>Chapter 12: Transcribing English to Japanese</li> </ul> <p>Grammar</p> <ul> <li>Chapter 13: Nouns</li> <li>Chapter 14: Verbs</li> <li>Chapter 15: Adjectives</li> <li>Chapter 16: Pro-forms</li> <li>Chapter 17: Telling time</li> <li>Chapter 18: Basic Particles</li> <li>Chapter 19: Sentence ending particles</li> <li>Chapter 20: Giving and Receiving</li> <li>Chapter 21: Comparisons</li> <li>Chapter 22: Simultaneous action</li> <li>Chapter 23: Transitivity</li> <li>Chapter 24: Verb conjugation table</li> <li>Chapter 25: Contents</li> </ul> <p>Vocabulary</p> <ul> <li>Chapter 26: Academic subjects</li> <li>Chapter 27: Animals</li> <li>Chapter 28: Banking</li> <li>Chapter 29: Body parts</li> <li>Chapter 30: Colors</li> <li>Chapter 31: Computing</li> <li>Chapter 32: Clothes and accessories</li> <li>Chapter 33: Countries, languages and nationalities</li> <li>Chapter 34: Direction</li> <li>Chapter 35: Family and people</li> <li>Chapter 36: Food and drink</li> <li>Chapter 37: Health</li> <li>Chapter 38: Numbers</li> <li>Chapter 39: Time</li> <li>Chapter 40: Dates</li> <li>Chapter 41: Weather and seasons</li> <li>Chapter 42: Vocabulary</li> </ul> <p>Linguistics</p> <ul> <li>Chapter 43: Pronunciation</li> <li>Chapter 44: Pitch accent</li> <li>Chapter 45: Dialects</li> <li>Chapter 46: Grammar</li> </ul>"},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-japanese/index.html#about-this-book","title":"About this book","text":"<p>A course in Japanese for English speakers: the writing systems (hiragana, katakana and kanji), pronunciation, particles, verbs and adjectives, politeness levels, vocabulary and conversation, with lessons and a grammar reference.</p> <p>From Wikibooks · CC BY-SA 4.0</p><p>Japanese, a Wikibooks textbook, by its contributors. This book is not stored in this library: each chapter is read from Wikibooks when it is opened, shown in this library's format, and ends with its own attribution. Licence: CC BY-SA 4.0. Modified: converted to this format.</p>"},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-japanese/about-2.html","title":"Chapter 2: About","text":""},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-japanese/about-2.html#21-introduction-welcome-to-the-japanese-wikibook","title":"2.1 Introduction - Welcome to the Japanese Wikibook","text":""},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-japanese/about-2.html#22-current-work","title":"2.2 Current work","text":""},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-japanese/academic-subjects.html","title":"Chapter 26: Academic subjects","text":""},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-japanese/adjectives.html","title":"Chapter 15: Adjectives","text":""},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-japanese/adjectives.html#151-basic-conjugations","title":"15.1 Basic conjugations","text":""},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-japanese/adjectives.html#152-more-forms","title":"15.2 More forms","text":""},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-japanese/adjectives.html#153-impera